From 2baa3bf909d9e54cc67eb4e8818e51ec97bdb065 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:33:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: config.txt is read by GET /api/boot-config only

Why: get_boot_config was a socket twin of the card's read route. Original
Apertar has two get_ commands only (get_state, get_media_test_state) and no
command twin for a file the browser shows: GET /api/config is the one read
for the hardware file. Nothing called get_boot_config; only the README named
it.

What: the get_boot_config block and its name in the commands reply are gone,
and README names set_boot_config only. GET /api/boot-config is the one read,
so the nested reply lives on a read route, as /api/media does.
bootConfigGet no longer takes an id.

Tested: check_core.sh both tests (builds, 21 host tests, no new warning).
--simulate: the socket and /api/command answer get_boot_config with
"Unknown command: get_boot_config"; GET /api/boot-config is unchanged;
smoke_core shape diff: every base field present with the same type. The
commands reply loses one name that 1.6.0 does not have. Needs the camera:
nothing; a Pi check reads the card with curl -s localhost:8000/api/boot-config.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NEFc1w7Y8dcyiV489BiwMr
---
 README.md              |  2 +-
 src/ApertarCoreApp.cpp | 11 ++++-------
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 24e8e1d..527b550 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -214,7 +214,7 @@ If the camera does not come back after a change, put the card in a reader and co
 
 The card saves with the `set_boot_config` command through `POST /api/command`, the same door as every other setting; `GET /api/boot-config` reads the file.
 
-Socket commands: `get_boot_config`, and `set_boot_config` with `cam0_sensor`, `cam1_sensor`, `cam0_link_frequency`, `cam1_link_frequency`, `i2c`, `i2s`, `spi`, `audio`, `rp1`, `display`, plus `dry_run`, `revision` and `confirm_display`, and, only with `APERTAR_BOOT_CONFIG_TEXT=on`, `text` (the whole file as edited; the other fields go on top of it).
+Socket command: `set_boot_config` with `cam0_sensor`, `cam1_sensor`, `cam0_link_frequency`, `cam1_link_frequency`, `i2c`, `i2s`, `spi`, `audio`, `rp1`, `display`, plus `dry_run`, `revision` and `confirm_display`, and, only with `APERTAR_BOOT_CONFIG_TEXT=on`, `text` (the whole file as edited; the other fields go on top of it).
 
